The evidence points to an abrupt Codex host/session termination, not a repository or test failure: PID `9555` stopped without a graceful shutdown record, no crash report was written, and macOS logs show no Codex memory-pressure/jetsam kill. Its two pytest children were tied to that host and disappeared with it, so their partial results are unusable.

Recovery boundary:
- keep verified commits `aec165d` / integrated `7c41f71` / review `8dab04e`;
- retain the already-complete focused evidence: 142/142 on both runtimes, 25/25 materializer, static gates, and two no-finding reviews;
- rerun only the interrupted full 1,020-test repository suites, sequentially and detached from this session;
- then push the feature and scoped review branches and resume the Copilot PR loop.

I’m setting up that detached verification now so another session restart will not discard the test run.

